-\n\ntitle: Sample apps\nhide-feedback: true\n-------------------\n\n## Ras=
pberry Pi camera\n\nSensors publish their observations to Lattice as entiti=
es, and can expose a\nlive video feed and accept tasks that control their b=
ehavior. This sample app\nintegrates a Raspberry Pi camera with Lattice usi=
ng the Python gRPC (Connect)\nSDK, presenting the camera as a stationary as=
set with an electro-optical (EO)\nsensor.\n\nThe app runs as two systemd un=
its on the Pi. A Python daemon publishes the\nentity at 1 Hz, registers a l=
ive [SRT](https://www.haivision.com/products/srt-secure-reliable-transport/=
)\nvideo ingress, samples and reports health, and listens as a Lattice agen=
t for\ntwo custom tasks, `Start` and `Stop`. The second unit runs MediaMTX,=
 which\ncaptures the camera and pushes H.264 video over SRT to the ingress =
URL that\nLattice returns.\n\nThis app demonstrates how to combine several =
Lattice capabilities in a single\nintegration:\n\n* Publishing an asset ent=
ity with an EO sensor to let operators see\n  the camera and its field of v=
iew on the map.\n* Registering a live video ingress that delivers a viewabl=
e feed\n  alongside the entity in Lattice.\n* Listening for and executing c=
ustom tasks to let operators control the\n  camera, by starting and stoppin=
g the video feed.\n* Reporting real-time health to let operators know wheth=
er the\n  camera and its feed are working.\n\n&lt;Accordion title=3D\&quot;=
Raspberry Pi camera\&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;Note&gt;\n    Click to go to the samp=
le application repository on GitHub. By downloading and/or using, you agree=
 to the terms of use.\n    If you do not agree, do not use the application =
or the SDK:\n  &lt;/Note&gt;\n\n  * [Raspberry Pi camera sample app](https:=
//github.com/anduril/sample-app-camera)\n&lt;/Accordion&gt;\n\n## Entity vi=
sualizer\n\nEntities characterize real world objects such as vehicles, ship=
s, aircraft, and\nmore. The Lattice data model provides an open, flexible s=
et of attributes\nwhich may be defined by automated sensor systems, tactica=
l data links, and input\nby human operators. This sample app renders a simp=
le web app\nwhich shows all entities in an environment on a map.\n\nThis ap=
p is designed to be a starting point for learning about entities and the ma=
ny attributes enabled by\nthe entity open data model:\n\n&lt;Accordion titl=
e=3D\&quot;Entity visualizer\&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;Note&gt;\n    Click to go to=
 the sample application repository on GitHub. By downloading and/or using, =
you agree to the terms of use.\n    If you do not agree, do not use the app=
lication or the SDK:\n  &lt;/Note&gt;\n\n  * [Visualize Entities on a Map s=
ample app](https://github.com/anduril/sample-app-entity-visualizer)\n&lt;/A=
ccordion&gt;\n\n&lt;Frame background=3D\&quot;subtle\&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;img =
src=3D\&quot;file:assets/images/sample-apps/entity-map.png\&quot; /&gt;\n&l=
t;/Frame&gt;\n\n## Task an asset\n\nTasks are the core open data model whic=
h communicate requests to manned or\nunmanned agents to perform purposeful =
activities, such as moving to a given\nlocation, orienting sensing towards =
a location of interest, or taking more\nactive actions on other entities.\n=
\nThis repository demonstrates how to define and operate on a custom `Orbit=
` task.\nThe task is defined in a `.proto` file and published to the Lattic=
e Schema Registry.\n\nThree distinct programs demonstrate:\n\n* Publishing =
a Track to Lattice representing a sensor point-of-interests\n* Creating a t=
askable Asset that accepts and executes an `Orbit` task\n* Using the Common=
 Operating Picture (COP) to identify and automatically task the Asset based=
 on\n  the entities in the environment.\n\nThese work in conjunction to dem=
onstrate an automated tasking scenario.\n\nYou can download this sample app=
 from GitHub.\n\n&lt;Accordion title=3D\&quot;Auto reconnaissance\&quot;&gt=
;\n  &lt;Note&gt;\n    Click to go to the sample application repository on =
GitHub. By downloading and/or using, you agree to the terms of use.\n    If=
 you do not agree, do not use the application or the SDK:\n  &lt;/Note&gt;\=
n\n  * [Task an Asset sample app](https://github.com/anduril/sample-app-aut=
o-reconnaissance)\n&lt;/Accordion&gt;\n\n&lt;Frame background=3D\&quot;subt=
le\&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;img src=3D\&quot;file:assets/images/sample-apps/taskin=
g.png\&quot; /&gt;\n&lt;/Frame&gt;\n\n## Objects CLI\n\nIn Lattice, the [Ob=
jects API](/reference/rest/objects/list-objects) provides a content-deliver=
y\nnetwork service that enables resilient data storage at the edge. This sa=
mple app implements\na command-line interface that lets developers interact=
 with the Objects API for managing\nfiles across the Lattice environment.\n=
\nThe Objects CLI provides a comprehensive set of operations including uplo=
ading files with\ncustomizable time-to-live values, downloading objects to =
specified locations, retrieving metadata,\nlisting objects with prefix filt=
ering, and deleting objects from the store.\n\n&lt;Accordion title=3D\&quot=
;Objects CLI\&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;Note&gt;\n    Click to go to the sample appl=
ication repository on GitHub. By downloading and/or using, you agree to the=
 terms of use.\n    If you do not agree, do not use the application or the =
SDK:\n  &lt;/Note&gt;\n\n  * [Objects CLI sample app](https://github.com/an=
duril/sample-app-objects)\n&lt;/Accordion&gt;\n\n&lt;Frame background=3D\&q=
uot;subtle\&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;img src=3D\&quot;file:assets/images/sample-app=
s/objects-cli.png\&quot; /&gt;\n&lt;/Frame&gt;\n\nFor more information, see=
 [Objects overview](/guides/objects/overview).\n\n## Integrate maritime AIS=
 position data\n\nThe AIS (Automatic Identification System) vessel traffic =
dataset is a repository\nof vessel identification and positioning data. The=
 data is collected by the U.S.\nCoast Guard through an onboard navigation s=
afety device that transmits and\nmonitors the location and characteristics =
of vessels in U.S. and international\nwaters in real time.\n\nThis sample i=
ntegration utilizes previously extracted AIS\ndata to represent the locatio=
n of a surface vessel over time, and then models\nthat vessel as an entity =
with a location which is periodically updated. Once the\nentity is publishe=
d in Lattice it may be visualized or referenced by another\napp.\n\nThis sa=
mple app is available using the gRPC SDK or the REST SDK:\n\n&lt;Accordion =
title=3D\&quot;AIS integration\&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;Note&gt;\n    Click to go =
to the sample application repository on GitHub. By downloading and/or using=
, you agree to the terms of use.\n    If you do not agree, do not use the a=
pplication or the SDK:\n  &lt;/Note&gt;\n\n  * [AIS Integration sample app =
using gRPC SDK](https://github.com/anduril/sample-app-ais-integration-grpc)=
\n  * [AIS Integration sample app using REST SDK](https://github.com/anduri=
l/sample-app-ais-integration-rest)\n&lt;/Accordion&gt;\n\n&lt;Frame backgro=
und=3D\&quot;subtle\&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;img src=3D\&quot;file:assets/images/s=
ample-apps/ais-motion.png\&quot; /&gt;\n&lt;/Frame&gt;\n\n## Entity thumbna=
il\n\nIn Lattice, an object is a data model that lets you store and access =
files across your environment.\nThe [**Objects**](/reference/rest/objects/l=
ist-objects) API is a content-delivery network service that provides resili=
ent data storage at the edge.\nUse objects together with entities to implem=
ent use-cases like track thumbnails, and vessel manifests.\n\nThis app demo=
nstrates an entity thumbnail use-case implemented with the Lattice SDK. The=
 sample app is a command-line interface\ntool that lets you upload images t=
o Lattice, and link them with an entity. The example C2 app shows this link=
ed image as a thumbnail\nof the entity:\n\n&lt;Accordion title=3D\&quot;Tra=
ck thumbnail\&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;Note&gt;\n    Click to go to the sample appl=
ication repository on GitHub. By downloading and/or using, you agree to the=
 terms of use.\n    If you do not agree, do not use the application or the =
SDK:\n  &lt;/Note&gt;\n\n  * [Entity thumbnail sample app](https://github.c=
om/anduril/sample-app-thumbnail)\n&lt;/Accordion&gt;\n\n&lt;Frame backgroun=
d=3D\&quot;subtle\&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;img src=3D\&quot;file:assets/images/sam=
ple-apps/track-thumbnail.png\&quot; /&gt;\n&lt;/Frame&gt;\n\nFor more infor=
mation, see [Objects](/guides/objects/overview).\n&quot;],&quot;perViewerCo=
py&quot;:[0,true],&quot;askAiEnabled&quot;:[0,false],&quot;skillsConfig&quo=
