or" stroke-width=3D"2" stroke-linecap=3D"round" stroke-linejoin=3D"round" c=
lass=3D"lucide lucide-external-link external-link-icon"><path d=3D"M15 3h6v=
6"></path><path d=3D"M10 14 21 3"></path><path d=3D"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H=
5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"></path></svg></a>
video ingress, samples and reports health, and listens as a Lattice agent f=
or
two custom tasks, <code>Start</code> and <code>Stop</code>. The second unit=
 runs MediaMTX, which
captures the camera and pushes H.264 video over SRT to the ingress URL that
Lattice returns.</p>
<p>This app demonstrates how to combine several Lattice capabilities in a s=
ingle
integration:</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;&gt;li]:relative [&amp;&gt;li]:before:text-(color:--gray=
scale-a10) mb-3 list-none pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:abso=
lute [&amp;&gt;li]:before:ml-[-22px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:mt-[-1px] [&amp;&=
gt;li]:before:content-['=E2=A6=81'] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:self-center">
<li class=3D"">Publishing an asset entity with an EO sensor to let operator=
s see
the camera and its field of view on the map.</li>
<li class=3D"">Registering a live video ingress that delivers a viewable fe=
ed
alongside the entity in Lattice.</li>
<li class=3D"">Listening for and executing custom tasks to let operators co=
ntrol the
camera, by starting and stopping the video feed.</li>
<li class=3D"">Reporting real-time health to let operators know whether the
camera and its feed are working.</li>
</ul>
