<h2 id=3D"task-an-asset" class=3D"max-md:pr-4" data-state=3D"closed" style=
=3D"cursor: pointer;">Task an asset</h2>
<p>Tasks are the core open data model which communicate requests to manned =
or
unmanned agents to perform purposeful activities, such as moving to a given
location, orienting sensing towards a location of interest, or taking more
active actions on other entities.</p>
<p>This repository demonstrates how to define and operate on a custom <code=
>Orbit</code> task.
The task is defined in a <code>.proto</code> file and published to the Latt=
ice Schema Registry.</p>
<p>Three distinct programs demonstrate:</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;&gt;li]:relative [&amp;&gt;li]:before:text-(color:--gray=
scale-a10) mb-3 list-none pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:abso=
lute [&amp;&gt;li]:before:ml-[-22px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:mt-[-1px] [&amp;&=
gt;li]:before:content-['=E2=A6=81'] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:self-center">
<li class=3D"">Publishing a Track to Lattice representing a sensor point-of=
-interests</li>
<li class=3D"">Creating a taskable Asset that accepts and executes an <code=
>Orbit</code> task</li>
<li class=3D"">Using the Common Operating Picture (COP) to identify and aut=
omatically task the Asset based on
the entities in the environment.</li>
</ul>
<p>These work in conjunction to demonstrate an automated tasking scenario.<=
/p>
<p>You can download this sample app from GitHub.</p>
